T*
(Marlin Test 01 - Exercise 001. When did the vessel arrive?) Tj
T*
(Passage:) Tj
T*
(The vessel arrived at Port Alpha at 0700. Cargo inspection began at 0800 and finished at) Tj
T*
(1030. All seals were intact. Departure was scheduled for 1400.) Tj
T*
(Options:) Tj
T*
(- 0800) Tj
T*
(- 1400) Tj
T*
(- 0700) Tj
T*
(- 1030) Tj
T*
(CORRECT ANSWER: 0700) Tj
T*
(Explanation: The answer is stated in the passage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(QUESTION 2 | MARLIN TEST 1 | READING) Tj
T*
(Marlin Test 01 - Exercise 005. What should happen to plastic waste?) Tj
T*
(Passage:) Tj
T*
(The vessel uses separate bins for food waste, plastics and metal. Crew must follow the waste) Tj
T*
(plan. Plastic waste must never be thrown overboard.) Tj
T*
(Options:) Tj
T*
(- It should be mixed with food waste) Tj
T*
(- It should be kept for proper disposal) Tj
T*
(- It should be thrown into the sea) Tj
T*
(- It should be burned on deck) Tj
T*
(CORRECT ANSWER: It should be kept for proper disposal) Tj
T*
(Explanation: The answer is stated in the passage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(QUESTION 3 | MARLIN TEST 1 | READING) Tj
T*
(Marlin Test 01 - Exercise 006. What was included in the handover?) Tj
T*
(Passage:) Tj
T*
(At 1800, the second officer handed over the watch. He explained the vessel's position,) Tj
T*
(nearby traffic, weather and equipment defects. The incoming officer repeated key details.) Tj
T*
(Options:) Tj
T*
(- Position, traffic, weather and defects) Tj
T*
(- Only the meal schedule) Tj
T*
(- Only crew leave plans) Tj
T*
(- Only cargo prices) Tj
T*
(CORRECT ANSWER: Position, traffic, weather and defects) Tj
T*
(Explanation: The answer is stated in the passage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(QUESTION 4 | MARLIN TEST 1 | READING) Tj
T*
(Marlin Test 01 - Exercise 002. What did the engineer do after noticing the leak?) Tj
T*
(Passage:) Tj
T*
(The duty engineer noticed a small leak near a pump. He informed the chief engineer, placed a) Tj
T*
(warning sign and isolated the pump. Repairs began when a spare seal arrived.) Tj
